## Summary

`@tailwindcss/webpack` and `@tailwindcss/turbopack` return a stylesheet unprocessed when `@variant` is the only Tailwind CSS feature it uses:

```css
.btn {
  color: black;
  @variant hover {
    color: red;
  }
}
```

Both loaders output the `@variant hover { … }` block as is. With Turbopack, Next.js then warns `Unknown at rule: @variant`. `@tailwindcss/postcss` turns it into `&:hover { @media (hover: hover) { … } }`.

The loaders skip a file unless its compiler features include `AtApply | JsPluginCompat | ThemeFunction | Utilities`. `Features.Variants` is not in that list. `@tailwindcss/vite` had the same problem and fixed it in #19966. This PR adds `Features.Variants` to both loaders.

## Test plan

- Added `@tailwindcss/webpack loader with only @variant` to `integrations/webpack/loader.test.ts` and `@tailwindcss/turbopack loader with only @variant (dev)` to `integrations/turbopack/loader.test.ts`. Both fail without the fix and pass with it.
- `pnpm vitest --root=./integrations run webpack/ turbopack/`: all tests pass.
- `pnpm vitest run`: all tests pass.
- `pnpm changelog check` and `prettier --check` pass.

